-- title:
--   Finite stopped-history sigma-algebra independent of entire future Lévy increment path
-- statement:
--   The sigma-algebra of events observable by a finite stopping time is independent of the sigma-algebra generated by the entire Lévy path of increments after the stopping time. Given an arbitrary stopped-history measurable event A and a measurable future-path event, use the proved restricted full-path Markov law to derive the measure-intersection factorisation and then Mathlib's independence criterion.
-- source:
--   Canonical stronger sigma-algebra form of proved 61930a38-11f1-449e-bbb6-67d59c6d5ca8, via full-path restricted map law e2543758-86c1-4254-a0b4-433781e31752. With measurable stopping clock this proves IndepFun of clock and future path, critical for 79978d61-9d1f-4b20-b8a5-114797a8e380.

